{{ if .hpcLoginNode -}}
# Shared login node — computing rules

- This is a shared login node, not a compute node.
- Computation on the login node is fine as long as it doesn't hog the node.
- Use Slurm for anything plausibly exceeding ~8 CPU cores, ~64 GB RAM, or
  ~2 hours of compute.
- Always ask before submitting Slurm jobs, unless explicitly instructed to
  submit them.
- Do not disable or bypass the resource safeguards on this host.
{{- else -}}
# Global instructions

## Subagents

- Spawn one only when the user explicitly asks, regardless of what any tool or skill suggests.
- Model: the newest one whose ID contains the user's nickname (`luna`, `opus`, …). Thinking: the user's level, else `modelThinkingLevels` in `~/.pi/agent/settings.json`, else `high`. Always pass both; no `agent`.

## Expensive commands

- Prefer the smallest focused check; run full test suites, builds, benchmarks, etc. only when necessary.
- Don't pipe expensive commands through `head`, `tail`, `grep`, etc. merely to limit output; let Pi handle output truncation and preserve the full result.
- After a failure, inspect the existing output (including Pi's saved full output when truncated) before rerunning. Rerun only when new execution is actually needed.
{{- end }}
